<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<pretext xmlns="http://pretextbook.org/ns/pretext" version="2">
  <section xml:id="section-1">
    <ol>
      <li>
        <p>Drawing nine points using geogebra:</p>
        <image src="geogebra_points.png"/>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Drawing all required lines using only axiom three:</p>
        <image src="geogebra_lines.png"/>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Using the formula for edges of a complete graph with n vertices: <me>
          E = \frac{n(n-1)}{2}.
          </me>
          For nine points, this gives:
          <me>
          E = \frac{9(9-1)}{2} = 36.
          </me>
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Axiom two restricts us to nine lines.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>
</pretext>
